title ALES143 — Lotus's stereo_infinite_clip: the infinite clipper carried into stereo, closing the dead-zone family in stereo, the rail that holds phase yet collapses ratio
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Third lap of this recur turn (after ALES141 stereo_center_clip and ALES142 stereo_soft_center_clip). The ALES142 log named ALES89 infinite_clip into stereo as the finishing edge that closes the dead-zone family; crux-first, I took it — closing a clean three-member arc is a satisfying finishing edge.
think ALES89's infinite_clip is y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else sign(x)·sample_max — silence the dead zone, then pin every survivor to the rail (a sine becomes a square). It is the third reading of the survivor's fate: hard PASSES, soft SHIFTS, infinite PINS. Carried into stereo it holds and breaks a distinct trio of laws: ODD, so the antisymmetry HOLDS (out-of-phase stays out of phase); but every survivor is slammed to the same magnitude, so the ratio COLLAPSES to unity (a 1:2 master comes back 1:1 — the extreme beyond the soft clip's mere break); and thresh = 0 is NOT the identity here but the PURE COMPARATOR (every nonzero sample pins, only exact silence survives), where for the two center clips thresh = 0 was the identity. Idempotence holds on [0, sample_max − 1]; the honest edge at t = sample_max (the pinned survivor itself falling back into the dead zone) is stated, not exercised.
think Proved all of it: the stereo law against ALES89's own mono run, antisymmetry held (r[i] = −l[i]), ratio collapsed (asserted r == l, not 2l, on a 1:2 master), idempotence below the rail, the pure-comparator at thresh = 0 by hand on both channels (sign preserved, only exact 0 surviving), the family bond against ALES141's stereo_center_clip (same dead zone silenced, survivors pinned to the rail with the same sign where hard passed), identical-channel identity, span discipline, and both faults atomic. The negative rail is −sample_max on purpose (odd symmetry over one LSB), the two's-complement care carried from ALES89. InfiniteClipError reused whole.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo dead-zone corner now stands WHOLE (ALES141 hard · ALES142 soft · ALES143 infinite), a clean three-way reading of the survivor's fate that pairs with the DRIVE family's ceiling clippers. The honest lesson across the three: the mask (hard) preserves ratio and phase and is idempotent; the shift (soft) preserves only phase; the rail (infinite) preserves phase but collapses ratio to unity and turns thresh = 0 into a comparator. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean. Three rounds landed and sent this turn (ALES141–143), a good finishing edge. The next Lotus lap opens a fresh direction (a new mono primitive or another corner into stereo) — a check-in-worthy choice of heading rather than a mechanical continuation.
